# svGolf PINNED scoring flow, stage 2 of 2: SYNTHESIS AND MEASUREMENT (Yosys +
# ABC). Do not edit: a change here is a change to every score. score.py fills
# the @NAME@ placeholders and records this file's sha256 (`script_sha256`) in
# every result. It runs in a fresh Yosys process on the canonical RTLIL that
# stage 1 (canon.ys) wrote.
#
#   @RTLIL@    the canonical RTLIL from stage 1
#   @TOP@      the task's top module
#   @STAT@     output file for `stat -json` (gate counts by type)
#   @LTP@      output file for `ltp -noff` (longest topological path)
#   @NETLIST@  output file: the scored gate netlist (`write_verilog -noexpr`:
#              one `$_AND_`/`$_MUX_`/... instance per scored gate), which the
#              checker's `postsynth` stage simulates. It is written AFTER
#              `stat` and `ltp`, so it cannot influence the score.
#
# Area is the gate count weighted by ge.json (NAND2 gate equivalents); depth is
# the `ltp` length, the number of gates on the longest input-to-output path.
read_rtlil @RTLIL@
synth -flatten -top @TOP@
abc -g AND,NAND,OR,NOR,XOR,XNOR,ANDNOT,ORNOT,MUX
opt_clean
tee -q -o @STAT@ stat -json
tee -q -o @LTP@ ltp -noff
write_verilog -noattr -noexpr @NETLIST@
